OpenMP Lecture 1 companion programs
-----------------------------------
hello0.c   Frame 2. One parallel region, printf only, no omp.h. Built twice:
           without -fopenmp (gcc -Wall warns "ignoring #pragma omp parallel"
           and the program prints one line) and with -fopenmp
           (OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 ./hello0 prints four lines).
           Outputs are deterministic; the frame needs no Centaurus run.
hello.c    Frame 4. Parallel region; each thread prints "Hello world from
           thread N of p" using omp_get_thread_num() and omp_get_num_threads().
           Run with OMP_NUM_THREADS=4. Line order varies between runs
           (10 distinct orders in 100 sandbox runs).
threads.c  Frame 5. Three regions; thread 0 of each reports the team size.
           OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 ./threads gives 4, 3, 2 (environment, then
           omp_set_num_threads(3), then the num_threads(2) clause).
           TO MEASURE on gal-c1: ./threads with OMP_NUM_THREADS unset; the
           frame states the gcc default of one thread per core (36) as [TBD].
